course: dictionary
lesson: 192
title: Airliners in the sky
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: An airliner is a large aeroplane that carries passengers on regular flights for an airline. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context. The words around airliner here are engines, pilots and flights, so it must be a big flying machine.
explain: «Most airliners have 2 engines, and some very big ones have 4.» Engines tell you the airliner is a powered aircraft. «Pilots fly with a stick or yoke, pedals and throttles, and read screens showing speed, height and direction» tells you what it takes to fly one.
explain: Look for phrases too. A jet airliner has jet engines, a passenger airliner carries people, and a jumbo jet is a big airliner. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: An airliner is a large aeroplane that carries passengers on regular flights for an airline.
fact: Most airliners have 2 engines, and some very big ones have 4.
fact: A jet engine sucks air in with a big fan, squeezes it, burns fuel in it and blasts hot gas out of the back.
fact: In a modern airliner engine, most of the push comes from the big fan at the front.
fact: An airliner always has two pilots.
exercise: What is an airliner? | *A large aeroplane that carries passengers on regular flights for an airline | A train that runs under the ground | A tiny toy aeroplane for children | A boat that carries cars across the sea
exercise: «An airliner always has two pilots.» How many pilots does an airliner always have? | One | Three | Four | *Two
exercise: In a modern airliner engine, which part gives most of the push? | *The big fan at the front | The tail | The back of the engine, where the hot gas comes out | The wings
test: Why do many airlines serve different meals to the two pilots? | Because pilots only like certain foods | *So that one bad meal cannot make both pilots ill | To make the flight take longer | So that the pilots can sleep during the flight
test: What is a jumbo jet? | A pilot's control stick | A kind of jet fuel | *A big airliner | A small glider with no engine
exam: Which is the best definition of an airliner? | A small private plane flown by one pilot | A tiny toy aeroplane for children | *A large aeroplane that carries passengers on regular flights for an airline | A boat that carries cars across the sea
